Context: T101, plan 004 S2 (skip per-pass work for unchanged sources). Design choices: the skip state is the (identity, size, modtime) probe triple held in memory per Watcher, not a new checkpoint field, so no state-format change and a restart degrades to one full verification pass instead of trusting persisted mtimes; the triple moves with a rename rebind and is dropped for missing paths. RegisterSource is gated by an in-process sourceID->path map rather than hub state because device and agent are fixed per ingestor process; a fresh process re-registers every source once, and ErrSourceNotRegistered from the write path deletes the map entry so a hub restored from a backup heals on the next pass (pinned by TestIngestReRegistersSourceAfterHubLosesRow). Accepted edge, unchanged from before: an in-place rewrite that restores exact size and mtime is invisible until restart (NOTES.md). Measurement evidence: perf/t101/ (gitignored) and docs/performance.md "Idle ingestion cost" - rchar 176,038,235 B to 330 B per 60 s window over 1,482 sources, storage reads 0 both ways; live append still detected end to end on the changed binary.
